{"seq":1,"mint":"C11","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"it is an entry in SNAPSHOT_FILES and therefore ships into `<memo>.tetel/` with every render.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F22"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"/// Existing files are overwritten: re-rendering a memo replaces its\n/// snapshot, since the snapshot's whole purpose is to match the memo\n/// currently on disk. A file absent from the workspace is skipped rather\n/// than erroring — a workspace with no refusals has no refusals log.","why":"The captured behavior explicitly skips an absent `refusals.log`, so it does not ship with every render.","quoted":true},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"a new workspace file is withheld by default and ships only when someone adds a line with a justifying comment beside every other entry's.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F22"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"    \"transplants.jsonl\",\n    \"counters.json\",\n    \"pending.json\",\n    \"refusals.log\",\n    // Without this, `check` cannot tell who authored the memo, and so","why":"The captured list has consecutive entries without a justifying comment beside them, contradicting the assertion that every other entry has one.","quoted":true}],"at":1790153560,"cost":0.00337242,"elapsed_ms":38892,"attempts":4,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":2,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":1}
